            <div xml:id="d1686">

                <pb facs="1376" n="1260" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1260"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No 419.11 D 29/32.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American Chargé
                        d’Affaires</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-11-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 23, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your No. 240, of the 1st
                    instant, I desire to say that the Department is glad to learn of the apparently
                    sincere determination of the present administration of Panama to identify and
                    punish those responsible for the killing and wounding of American citizens in
                    Panama on July 4 last, and trusts that the investigation which has been
                    undertaken will lead to prompt results along this line.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
